WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:02.600
- On April 15, 2011, I spent my

00:00:02.600 --> 00:00:07.330
21st birthday in jail, this is that story.

00:00:07.330 --> 00:00:09.500
Thankfully I can laugh at this story now,

00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:11.880
but there was some real
serious consequences

00:00:11.880 --> 00:00:13.910
that are still following me to this day.

00:00:13.910 --> 00:00:16.470
If you're turning 21, have fun but

00:00:16.470 --> 00:00:20.990
please, please please
be smart, here we go.

00:00:20.990 --> 00:00:23.150
So, I was a student at the
University of Oklahoma,

00:00:23.150 --> 00:00:25.470
and they are very strict about drinking.

00:00:25.470 --> 00:00:27.150
I mean, the whole state of Oklahoma is.

00:00:27.150 --> 00:00:29.590
I'm not hating on
Oklahoma, I loved Oklahoma.

00:00:29.590 --> 00:00:31.110
I loved going to school there,

00:00:31.110 --> 00:00:33.440
the state itself was beautiful and

00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:37.210
I was turning 21 and I was stoked to

00:00:37.210 --> 00:00:40.330
graduate from house parties to bar crawls.

00:00:40.330 --> 00:00:43.770
Not only was I turning
21, I was turning 21

00:00:43.770 --> 00:00:47.600
on a Friday which I thought
was totally awesome.

00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:49.280
Campus Corner Thursday night,

00:00:49.280 --> 00:00:51.160
birthday dinner and party Friday night,

00:00:51.160 --> 00:00:52.670
hanging out and playing video games

00:00:52.670 --> 00:00:54.290
with friends the rest of the weekend.

00:00:54.290 --> 00:00:56.410
It's my 21st birthday, I know I'm gonna be

00:00:56.410 --> 00:00:58.860
a little bit irresponsible so I at least

00:00:58.860 --> 00:01:01.300
wanted to do one responsible
thing that night.

00:01:01.300 --> 00:01:02.860
I parked my car at my buddy's place,

00:01:02.860 --> 00:01:04.950
who lived a couple of
blocks from Campus Corner,

00:01:04.950 --> 00:01:06.810
so that way we could walk from his house,

00:01:06.810 --> 00:01:08.060
party it up, and then I could just

00:01:08.060 --> 00:01:09.440
crash on his couch that night.

00:01:09.440 --> 00:01:10.730
So it's the night of my birthday,

00:01:10.730 --> 00:01:12.460
my car is parked, me and my friends

00:01:12.460 --> 00:01:13.510
we shimmy over to my favorite

00:01:13.510 --> 00:01:15.710
taco spot on Campus Corner, Fuzzy's,.

00:01:15.710 --> 00:01:18.970
We let our bellies full
of dang tacos, some queso.

00:01:18.970 --> 00:01:20.210
Okay, so when you think about it,

00:01:20.210 --> 00:01:21.530
it's kinda weird that we celebrated

00:01:21.530 --> 00:01:23.540
our 21st birthday by seeing how much

00:01:23.540 --> 00:01:26.270
alcohol we could consume
before blacking out.

00:01:26.270 --> 00:01:27.960
That's like turning 16 years old,

00:01:27.960 --> 00:01:30.450
and saying oh boy, I'm gonna get

00:01:30.450 --> 00:01:33.210
six cars and speed 120 miles an hour

00:01:33.210 --> 00:01:35.620
down the highway 'cause I got my license.

00:01:35.620 --> 00:01:38.340
The plan of tacos and queso was great.

00:01:38.340 --> 00:01:40.190
It lasted me through three margaritas

00:01:40.190 --> 00:01:41.620
and a couple of tequila shots.

00:01:41.620 --> 00:01:42.840
At this point, I was starting to

00:01:42.840 --> 00:01:44.670
enter the brownout phase, which in

00:01:44.670 --> 00:01:46.830
Clark's dictionary means the moments

00:01:46.830 --> 00:01:48.500
leading up to inevitable blackout.

00:01:48.500 --> 00:01:50.340
So after the clock strikes midnight and

00:01:50.340 --> 00:01:53.390
I am officially 21, I get
a call from my sister,

00:01:53.390 --> 00:01:56.410
which I don't remember and she said

00:01:56.410 --> 00:02:00.570
I was very, very, very, very excited,

00:02:00.570 --> 00:02:03.630
like Tom Cruise jumping
on a couch excited.

00:02:03.630 --> 00:02:05.620
- Katie once told Seventeen Magazine-

00:02:05.620 --> 00:02:06.620
- Yes!

00:02:06.620 --> 00:02:11.610
- Midnight to 1:45 a.m. are a little hazy.

00:02:11.610 --> 00:02:14.720
But when I finally reentered my body,

00:02:14.720 --> 00:02:19.720
I was peeing in a parking lot,
peeing on the parking lot.

00:02:20.970 --> 00:02:22.610
Here's Fuzzy's, the taco place,

00:02:22.610 --> 00:02:25.410
here's my car, here's Clark, maybe

00:02:25.410 --> 00:02:27.760
a quarter mile from his apartment

00:02:27.760 --> 00:02:29.560
peeing in the middle of a parking lot.

00:02:29.560 --> 00:02:31.850
And I forgot to mention, but uh,

00:02:31.850 --> 00:02:34.980
this just wasn't some like
random hidden parking lot,

00:02:34.980 --> 00:02:38.200
this was a church parking lot.

00:02:38.200 --> 00:02:41.330
I am peeing in God's parking lot.

00:02:41.330 --> 00:02:44.000
In my head, I'm in the clear,

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:46.370
'bout to finish my leak,
everything went pretty well,

00:02:46.370 --> 00:02:48.670
and then I see these
tinges of blue and red

00:02:48.670 --> 00:02:50.210
out of the corner of my eye and

00:02:50.210 --> 00:02:53.830
I hear a deep booming voice,
you all right there, buddy?

00:02:53.830 --> 00:02:58.830
Shit, yep, it's the cops, so I'm

00:03:00.530 --> 00:03:03.480
pleading with them in some sort of

00:03:03.480 --> 00:03:06.540
mumbled gibberish, tellin' 'em how it's my

00:03:06.540 --> 00:03:09.610
21st birthday and how I did a really

00:03:09.610 --> 00:03:13.470
responsible thing, (slurring)
at least I didn't drive,

00:03:13.470 --> 00:03:17.160
at least I didn't drive,
in the cop car all the

00:03:17.160 --> 00:03:19.600
way through getting
processed through jail.

00:03:19.600 --> 00:03:24.600
Jail, yep, I was booked into IRL jail.

00:03:24.750 --> 00:03:28.340
Not the drunk tank, we're
talking Shawshank Redemption,

00:03:28.340 --> 00:03:32.330
Orange is the New Black, Oz level jail.

00:03:32.330 --> 00:03:34.330
And to add icing to my birthday cake,

00:03:34.330 --> 00:03:36.560
since I was arrested early Friday morning,

00:03:36.560 --> 00:03:39.040
I wasn't gonna see a judge until Monday.

00:03:39.040 --> 00:03:40.530
Which meant I wasn't just spending my

00:03:40.530 --> 00:03:43.120
birthday in jail, I was spending the

00:03:43.120 --> 00:03:46.610
entire birthday weekend in jail.

00:03:46.610 --> 00:03:50.900
At the time I didn't really
register how badly I screwed up.

00:03:50.900 --> 00:03:53.610
I didn't think that my phone
would be ringing nonstop,

00:03:53.610 --> 00:03:57.160
that I supposed to work at
the equipment cage on campus.

00:03:57.160 --> 00:03:59.170
There were classes that
I would be missing.

00:03:59.170 --> 00:04:01.930
At some point, late Thursday night,

00:04:01.930 --> 00:04:03.580
early Friday morning, I must've

00:04:03.580 --> 00:04:06.910
fallen asleep or blacked out or both.

00:04:06.910 --> 00:04:09.390
I woke up under a scratchy wool blanket,

00:04:09.390 --> 00:04:14.260
on a metal bunk bed, inside of
a withering, gray jail cell.

00:04:14.260 --> 00:04:16.320
And I was wearing what I think you could

00:04:16.320 --> 00:04:19.640
best describe as traffic cone orange

00:04:19.640 --> 00:04:22.270
like, nurse scrubs and crocs.

00:04:22.270 --> 00:04:25.330
This truly was prison and my heart

00:04:25.330 --> 00:04:29.010
started sinking into my chest, shit.

00:04:29.010 --> 00:04:33.353
Suddenly, I hear this
gravelly, Josh Brolin

00:04:33.353 --> 00:04:36.170
soundin' voice from the
other corner of the room,

00:04:36.170 --> 00:04:40.000
morning princess, sounds
like you had fun last night.

00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:45.000
I have a cell mate, of
course, I have a cell mate.

00:04:46.310 --> 00:04:49.940
So I turn my aching head
and I look at this dude,

00:04:49.940 --> 00:04:54.460
leathery skin, popcorn
kernel yellow teeth,

00:04:54.460 --> 00:04:58.470
sunken in cheeks, this
big bushy beard that

00:04:58.470 --> 00:05:01.010
I'm pretty certain you
could hide a knife in.

00:05:01.010 --> 00:05:03.810
Great, this is it, this is jail.

00:05:03.810 --> 00:05:05.840
I was locked in here with my cell mate.

00:05:05.840 --> 00:05:07.590
No one ever prepares you in life

00:05:07.590 --> 00:05:09.390
what to talk to a cell mate about.

00:05:09.390 --> 00:05:11.800
Who's your favorite
character on Parks and Rec?

00:05:11.800 --> 00:05:14.820
What's your favorite sports
team, how's the weather?

00:05:14.820 --> 00:05:16.771
Okay, so quick pause, because this is

00:05:16.771 --> 00:05:18.550
the part of the story that is disturbing

00:05:18.550 --> 00:05:20.300
and it involves animals and if you've

00:05:20.300 --> 00:05:21.770
seen any of the videos that I've been in,

00:05:21.770 --> 00:05:24.360
you know that I love
Corgis and kitties and

00:05:24.360 --> 00:05:26.470
little piggies and any other thing that's

00:05:26.470 --> 00:05:30.640
cute and adorable and I
really, really, really

00:05:30.640 --> 00:05:33.940
hate this next part of the
story, um so here we go.

00:05:33.940 --> 00:05:36.340
I decided to strike up a conversation and

00:05:36.340 --> 00:05:39.135
I asked him what're ya in here for?

00:05:39.135 --> 00:05:40.930
Please don't say murder, please don't

00:05:40.930 --> 00:05:42.750
say murder, please don't say murder.

00:05:42.750 --> 00:05:44.500
I got caught fuckin' a goat.

00:05:44.500 --> 00:05:48.500
What, my cell mate, the
guy that I'm locked in this

00:05:48.500 --> 00:05:53.500
little box with, is an
actual bestiality offender.

00:05:53.662 --> 00:05:56.800
I'd hoped that I was massively hung over,

00:05:56.800 --> 00:05:59.010
because the extent of
what I could actually say

00:05:59.010 --> 00:06:03.950
to him was something along
the lines of, gotcha.

00:06:03.950 --> 00:06:08.090
So I rolled back on my
back, stared up at the

00:06:09.330 --> 00:06:12.660
metal bunk bed and just sang myself

00:06:12.660 --> 00:06:17.357
Happy Birthday. ♪ Happy Birthday to you.

00:06:20.450 --> 00:06:23.090
Several hours pass and lunch finally came.

00:06:23.090 --> 00:06:25.730
I lined up, got my tray from
the correctional officer.

00:06:25.730 --> 00:06:28.540
It was some super stale
cornbread, this like,

00:06:28.540 --> 00:06:30.930
meaty goop that I don't
even think a dog would eat.

00:06:30.930 --> 00:06:33.420
I'm scanning around the room,

00:06:33.420 --> 00:06:35.680
I'm seein' these dudes with the

00:06:35.680 --> 00:06:40.680
long scraggly hair and
their big scraggly beards.

00:06:41.250 --> 00:06:44.860
I look just like these dudes.

00:06:44.860 --> 00:06:47.853
I'm hung over, I'm feeling like death,

00:06:48.890 --> 00:06:52.130
I'm looking like death, what
am I doing with my life?

00:06:52.130 --> 00:06:54.670
I could tell that it was
kinda turning to night

00:06:54.670 --> 00:06:57.210
because a little sliver of light that was

00:06:57.210 --> 00:06:58.900
coming through in each jail cell was

00:06:58.900 --> 00:07:02.700
turning from milky white
to this deep rich purple.

00:07:02.700 --> 00:07:04.720
Another correctional officer walks in and

00:07:04.720 --> 00:07:09.720
starts listing off names:
Davis, Johnson, McCaskill.

00:07:10.344 --> 00:07:12.460
(gloomy acoustic guitar music)

00:07:12.460 --> 00:07:15.090
McCaskill, is this good or bad?

00:07:15.090 --> 00:07:18.060
I followed the officer with hesitation,

00:07:18.060 --> 00:07:21.420
and then he told me that I was going to be

00:07:21.420 --> 00:07:24.740
having a webcam session with the judge.

00:07:24.740 --> 00:07:28.740
Holy shit, but you know, I had to keep it

00:07:28.740 --> 00:07:30.930
cool because you know, prison.

00:07:30.930 --> 00:07:32.890
I talked to the judge and she said that

00:07:32.890 --> 00:07:35.380
what I did was really, really stupid and

00:07:35.380 --> 00:07:37.380
not something to take lightly,

00:07:37.380 --> 00:07:39.150
but also not something to spend the

00:07:39.150 --> 00:07:41.730
entire weekend in jail for and

00:07:41.730 --> 00:07:43.300
that I would be released that night.

00:07:43.300 --> 00:07:47.510
I actually cried, I cried
in front of the judge.

00:07:47.510 --> 00:07:51.150
I was just so relieved and so happy.

00:07:51.150 --> 00:07:54.740
I sign my paperwork, get my belongings,

00:07:54.740 --> 00:07:58.270
get outta my God awful
crocs and my orange scrubs.

00:07:58.270 --> 00:08:01.700
So I walk outta jail, it's like seven p.m.

00:08:01.700 --> 00:08:03.790
But I'm still way too nervous to

00:08:03.790 --> 00:08:08.590
turn on my phone because I
had a lot of missed calls.

00:08:08.590 --> 00:08:12.900
I get to my car, I drive home, and

00:08:12.900 --> 00:08:17.900
I go to bed in my room
without a cell mate.

00:08:18.220 --> 00:08:21.217
And that's how I spent
my 21st birthday in jail.

00:08:21.217 --> 00:08:24.217
(soft guitar music)

